t\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test3.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 5\b5:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt\r\n       `\b``\b`.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg`\b``\b` f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs objects under a specified prefix and\r\n       bucket to files in a local directory by uploading the local files to\r\n       S3. Because of the -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter, all files matching the pattern\r\n       existing both in S3 and locally will be excluded from the sync. In this\r\n       example, the user syncs the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt to the local\r\n       current directory.  The local current directory contains the files\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains the\r\n       object t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg of a different size than the local t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket \\\r\n              --exclude \"*.jpg\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 6\b6:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl l\blo\boc\bca\bal\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs t\bto\bo t\bth\bhe\be s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt\r\n       s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd d\bdi\bir\bre\bec\bct\bto\bor\bry\by f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs files under a local directory to\r\n       objects under a specified prefix and bucket by downloading S3 objects.\r\n       This example uses the -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter flag to exclude a specified\r\n       directory and S3 prefix from the s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command.  In this example, the\r\n       user syncs the local current directory to the bucket\r\n       a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt.  The local current directory contains the files\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br/\b/t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt.  The bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt\r\n       contains the objects a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br/\b/t\bte\bes\bst\bt5\b5.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt1\b1.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/ . \\\r\n              --exclude \"*another/*\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          download: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test1.txt to test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 7\b7:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc a\bal\bll\bl o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs b\bbe\bet\btw\bwe\bee\ben\bn b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bts\bs i\bin\bn d\bdi\bif\bff\bfe\ber\bre\ben\bnt\bt r\bre\beg\bgi\bio\bon\bns\bs\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs files between two buckets in different\r\n       regions:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync s3://my-us-west-2-bucket s3://my-us-east-1-bucket \\\r\n              --source-region us-west-2 \\\r\n              --region us-east-1\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          download: s3://my-us-west-2-bucket/test1.txt to s3://my-us-east-1-bucket/test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 8\b8:\b: S\bSy\byn\bnc\bc t\bto\bo a\ban\bn S\bS3\b3 a\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bs p\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt\r\n\r\n       The following s\bsy\byn\bnc\bc command syncs the current directory to the access\r\n       point (m\bmy\bya\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bsp\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt):\r\n\r\n          aws s3 sync . s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          upload: test.txt to s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/test.txt\r\n          upload: test2.txt to s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/test2.txt\r\n\r\n                                                                        SYNC()\r\n"}}}
