 -\b--\b-c\bca\ba-\b-b\bbu\bun\bnd\bdl\ble\be (string)\r\n\r\n       The CA certificate bundle to use when verifying SSL certificates.\r\n       Overrides config/env settings.\r\n\r\n       -\b--\b-c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-r\bre\bea\bad\bd-\b-t\bti\bim\bme\beo\bou\but\bt (int)\r\n\r\n       The maximum socket read time in seconds. If the value is set to 0, the\r\n       socket read \n\u003ctruncated 784 of 10662 bytes from the middle of the output\u003e\n to a binary\r\n       blob f\bfi\bil\ble\beb\bb:\b:/\b//\b/ will always be treated as binary and use the file\r\n       contents directly regardless of the c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-b\bbi\bin\bna\bar\bry\by-\b-f\bfo\bor\brm\bma\bat\bt setting. When\r\n       using f\bfi\bil\ble\be:\b:/\b//\b/ the file contents will need to properly formatted for the\r\n       configured c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-b\bbi\bin\bna\bar\bry\by-\b-f\bfo\bor\brm\bma\bat\bt.\r\n\r\n       +\bo base64\r\n\r\n       +\bo raw-in-base64-out\r\n\r\n       -\b--\b-n\bno\bo-\b-c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-p\bpa\bag\bge\ber\br (boolean)\r\n\r\n       Disable cli pager for output.\r\n\r\n       -\b--\b-c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-a\bau\but\bto\bo-\b-p\bpr\bro\bom\bmp\bpt\bt (boolean)\r\n\r\n       Automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.\r\n\r\n       -\b--\b-n\bno\bo-\b-c\bcl\bli\bi-\b-a\bau\but\bto\bo-\b-p\bpr\bro\bom\bmp\bpt\bt (boolean)\r\n\r\n       Disable automatically prompt for CLI input parameters.\r\n\r\nE\bEX\bXA\bAM\bMP\bPL\bLE\bES\bS\r\n       N\bNO\bOT\bTE\bE:\b:\r\n          To use the following examples, you must have the AWS CLI installed\r\n          and configured. See the _\bG_\be_\bt_\bt_\bi_\bn_\bg _\bs_\bt_\ba_\br_\bt_\be_\bd _\bg_\bu_\bi_\bd_\be in the _\bA_\bW_\bS _\bC_\bL_\bI _\bU_\bs_\be_\br\r\n          _\bG_\bu_\bi_\bd_\be for more information.\r\n\r\n          Unless otherwise stated, all examples have unix-like quotation\r\n          rules. These examples will need to be adapted to your terminal's\r\n          quoting rules. See _\bU_\bs_\bi_\bn_\bg _\bq_\bu_\bo_\bt_\ba_\bt_\bi_\bo_\bn _\bm_\ba_\br_\bk_\bs _\bw_\bi_\bt_\bh _\bs_\bt_\br_\bi_\bn_\bg_\bs in the _\bA_\bW_\bS _\bC_\bL_\bI\r\n          _\bU_\bs_\be_\br _\bG_\bu_\bi_\bd_\be .\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 1\b1:\b: D\bDe\bel\ble\bet\bte\be a\ban\bn S\bS3\b3 o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bt\r\n\r\n       The following r\brm\bm command deletes a single s3 object:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 rm s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 2\b2:\b: D\bDe\bel\ble\bet\bte\be a\bal\bll\bl c\bco\bon\bnt\bte\ben\bnt\bts\bs i\bin\bn a\ba b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt\r\n\r\n       The following r\brm\bm command recursively deletes all objects under a\r\n       specified bucket and prefix when passed with the parameter -\b--\b-r\bre\bec\bcu\bur\brs\bsi\biv\bve\be.\r\n       In this example, the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt contains the objects\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt1\b1.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 rm s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket \\\r\n              --recursive\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test1.txt\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test2.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 3\b3:\b: D\bDe\bel\ble\bet\bte\be a\bal\bll\bl c\bco\bon\bnt\bte\ben\bnt\bts\bs i\bin\bn a\ba b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt,\b, e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt `\b``\b`.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg`\b``\b` f\bfi\bil\ble\bes\bs\r\n\r\n       The following r\brm\bm command recursively deletes all objects under a\r\n       specified bucket and prefix when passed with the parameter -\b--\b-r\bre\bec\bcu\bur\brs\bsi\biv\bve\be\r\n       while excluding some objects by using an -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter.  In this\r\n       example, the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt has the objects t\bte\bes\bst\bt1\b1.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and\r\n       t\bte\bes\bst\bt2\b2.\b.j\bjp\bpg\bg:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 rm s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/ \\\r\n              --recursive \\\r\n              --exclude \"*.jpg\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 4\b4:\b: D\bDe\bel\ble\bet\bte\be a\bal\bll\bl c\bco\bon\bnt\bte\ben\bnt\bts\bs i\bin\bn a\ba b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt,\b, e\bex\bxc\bce\bep\bpt\bt o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bts\bs u\bun\bnd\bde\ber\br t\bth\bhe\be\r\n       s\bsp\bpe\bec\bci\bif\bfi\bie\bed\bd p\bpr\bre\bef\bfi\bix\bx\r\n\r\n       The following r\brm\bm command recursively deletes all objects under a\r\n       specified bucket and prefix when passed with the parameter -\b--\b-r\bre\bec\bcu\bur\brs\bsi\biv\bve\be\r\n       while excluding all objects under a particular prefix by using an\r\n       -\b--\b-e\bex\bxc\bcl\blu\bud\bde\be parameter.  In this example, the bucket a\bam\bmz\bzn\bn-\b-s\bs3\b3-\b-d\bde\bem\bmo\bo-\b-b\bbu\buc\bck\bke\bet\bt\r\n       has the objects t\bte\bes\bst\bt1\b1.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt and a\ban\bno\bot\bth\bhe\ber\br/\b/t\bte\bes\bst\bt.\b.t\btx\bxt\bt:\r\n\r\n          aws s3 rm s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/ \\\r\n              --recursive \\\r\n              --exclude \"another/*\"\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          delete: s3://amzn-s3-demo-bucket/test1.txt\r\n\r\n       E\bEx\bxa\bam\bmp\bpl\ble\be 5\b5:\b: D\bDe\bel\ble\bet\bte\be a\ban\bn o\bob\bbj\bje\bec\bct\bt f\bfr\bro\bom\bm a\ban\bn S\bS3\b3 a\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bs p\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt\r\n\r\n       The following r\brm\bm command deletes a single object (m\bmy\byk\bke\bey\by) from the\r\n       access point (m\bmy\bya\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bsp\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt). :: The following r\brm\bm command deletes a\r\n       single object (m\bmy\byk\bke\bey\by) from the access point (m\bmy\bya\bac\bcc\bce\bes\bss\bsp\bpo\boi\bin\bnt\bt).\r\n\r\n          aws s3 rm s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/mykey\r\n\r\n       Output:\r\n\r\n          delete: s3://arn:aws:s3:us-west-2:123456789012:accesspoint/myaccesspoint/mykey\r\n\r\n                                                                          RM()\r\n"}}}
